{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":79625,"duration_api_ms":79155,"num_turns":8,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d66861f1-99b5-44d0-b78e-962ebb16f8b0","total_cost_usd":0.39955195,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30544,"cache_read_input_tokens":194782,"output_tokens":1994,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30544,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":7,"outputTokens":1994,"cacheReadInputTokens":194782,"cacheCreationInputTokens":30544,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.338176,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":48,"outputTokens":3242,"cacheReadInputTokens":221117,"cacheCreationInputTokens":18405,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.06137595,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Accept both documentation-fix amendments (error message text and doc comment clarification) as they address real inaccuracies. Reject both blocking amendments because the habitat/geometry probe suite, summary runner, and per-habitat debug output all exist in crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_habitat_geometry_probes.rs — the amendments appear to be describing a different (alkalinity-focused) change set.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-3-dd96264b","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: SMALL_MEDIA_CM2=500 and LARGE_MEDIA_CM2=4000 (line 292-293), making the ratio 8×, not 2×. The error message at line 497 reads '2× media should expand filter habitat area by >1.5×' which is objectively wrong. A developer debugging a failure would be misled about the test configuration. Simple, safe string fix."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-703dc756","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: configure_redox_baseline sets aeration.enabled=false (line 1101), the planted arm does not override this, but the inert arm explicitly sets aeration.enabled=true and intensity=0.6 (lines 1167-1168). The doc comment at line 1027 claims the comparison is 'about substrate geometry and root-zone effects' without acknowledging the aeration asymmetry. Adding a note that the inert arm also has aeration enabled (and explaining why this strengthens the test) makes the documentation technically accurate without changing any behavior."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-b63c4158","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment's claim that no habitat/geometry probes exist is factually incorrect. crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_habitat_geometry_probes.rs (1640 lines) contains all five required probes: biofilter_scaling (line 289), light_depth, habitat_fouling, substrate_redox (line ~1017), and equipment_scaling, plus the all_habitat_geometry_probes_summary runner (line 1561). The amendment appears to describe a different alkalinity-focused diff, not the actual habitat/geometry implementation."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-49996a37","decision":"reject","rationale":"The claim that per-habitat diagnostics are missing is incorrect. e2e_habitat_geometry_probes.rs contains format_habitat_debug (line 44) and dump_habitat_debug (line 133), which emit per-habitat biomass, colonizable area, and habitat modifiers. These are called at 11 locations throughout the probe suite (e.g., lines 464-465, 730-731, 886-888, 1226-1227, 1461-1462). The engine.rs and budget_helpers.rs files being aggregate-only is irrelevant — the bead's per-habitat diagnostic requirement is fulfilled by the harness-level debug functions."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"3195d8c3-017f-4054-9211-6fa968c5e7a2"}
